
================================================================================
 STAGE 0.  Re-verify the IF2 input object (so the coarse-graining starts from truth)
================================================================================
[0.1] 2 F'(x^2) - mu_fw(x) = 0  (0 => IF2's F is the unique adiabatic match)
[0.2] mu_fw(x->0) ~ x  ;  mu_fw(x->oo) -> 1
      => deep-MOND inertial force m*mu_fw*a -> m a^2/a0  (the a^2/a0 law).  INVERSION mu(0)=0<mu(inf)=1.

================================================================================
 STAGE 1.  COARSE-GRAIN STEP 1 — orbit-average the fast worldline (Milgrom eq 55 route)
================================================================================
[1.1] Orbit-average (circular) of IF2: radial EOM  m*mu_fw(a/a0)*a = dphi/dr.
      This is EXACTLY Milgrom eq (53)  mu(a/ao) a = dphi/dr  with  mu = mu_fw.
      => the orbit-averaged IF2 worldline = Milgrom's circular-orbit MI, mu=mu_fw.  [VERIFIED via 0.1]
[1.2] deep-MOND (orbit-averaged) v^4 = G*M*a0  ; v^4-GMa0 = 0  (0 => BTFR)

================================================================================
 STAGE 2.  COARSE-GRAIN STEP 2 — continuum: from many worldlines to fields (the DICTIONARY)
================================================================================
Coarse-grained objects from the IF2 congruence:
  u^mu(x) = local mean worldline 4-velocity (the dS-bath rest frame the IF2 a0/T_eff is read in)
  phi(x)  = collective acceleration potential; grad phi = MI response (a = |grad phi| on a test particle)
  rho(x)  = coarse-grained mass density (couples phi*rho)

================================================================================
 Q1.  Does the aether A_mu emerge as the MI preferred frame?
================================================================================
[Q1.1] unit-timelike u^mu (u.u=-1): EMERGES automatically (4-velocity). Matches A.A=-1 + lambda(A^2+1).
[Q1.2] preferred-frame ROLE: EMERGES — IF2's T_eff/a0/mu_fw are frame-dependent; u^mu IS that frame.
[Q1.3] aether KINETIC -(K_B/2) F^2  (F_{mu nu}=2 grad_[mu A_nu]):  test if produced.
        In IF2, u^mu enters ONLY as the frame in which |qddot| (hence T_eff, mu_fw) is evaluated.
        The IF2 worldline action has NO term ~ (grad u)^2: u is a BACKGROUND CLOCK, not a d.o.f.
        Orbit-average/continuum of -(m a0^2)F(|qddot_in_u|^2/a0^2) produces a SCALAR self-action of
        grad phi; it does NOT produce a Maxwell-type (grad_[mu u_nu])^2 kinetic term for u.
        => K_B is NOT produced.  The aether EMERGES as a frame (Q1.1-2) but its DYNAMICS (K_B F^2)
           does NOT emerge.  Q1 = PARTIAL: frame yes, propagating-aether-kinetic NO. [both-ways]

================================================================================
 Q2.  Does the Y^{3/2} deep-MOND term emerge with the SAME a0?  (the strongest test)
================================================================================
[Q2.1] EL flux of -(1/3)(1/a0)|grad phi|^3 : Matrix([[-g_x*sqrt(g_x**2 + g_y**2 + g_z**2)/a0, -g_y*sqrt(g_x**2 + g_y**2 + g_z**2)/a0, -g_z*sqrt(g_x**2 + g_y**2 + g_z**2)/a0]])
       MOND flux -(|grad phi|/a0) grad phi  : Matrix([[-g_x*sqrt(g_x**2 + g_y**2 + g_z**2)/a0, -g_y*sqrt(g_x**2 + g_y**2 + g_z**2)/a0, -g_z*sqrt(g_x**2 + g_y**2 + g_z**2)/a0]])
       difference = Matrix([[0, 0, 0]])  (0 => AQUAL flux IS the MOND flux EXACTLY)
[Q2.2] Y^{3/2} with Y=|grad phi|^2 :  Y^{3/2}-|grad phi|^3 = 0  (0 => Y^{3/2}=|grad phi|^3)
[Q2.3] a0 placement: the coarse-grained IF2 carries the SAME a0 (mu_fw's only scale) into the
        |grad phi|^3 coefficient -- exactly AeST's J->(.../a0)Y^{3/2} slot.  SAME a0. [MATCH]
[Q2.4] AeST prefactor 2 lambda_s/(3(1+lambda_s)) -> 2/3 in the screening limit lambda_s->inf (in J);
        the physical AQUAL prefactor (post field-redefinition) is 1/3, fixed by the EXACT flux
        match [Q2.1]. The POWER (3/2) and the 1/a0 SCALING are the convention-free matched facts.
       *** Q2 = MATCH on power Y^{3/2}, on a0 placement, on the EL flux (exact). ***
       CAVEAT (load-bearing): this is the SHARED deep-MOND attractor — both MI and MG reduce to
       AQUAL/BM84 in deep MOND (Milgrom eq 53: mu(a/ao)a=dphi/dr is the SAME rotation curve for
       BOTH classes). It pins the IR fixed point; it does NOT show the UV completions coincide.

================================================================================
 Q3.  Does the shift-symmetric scalar phi emerge?
================================================================================
[Q3.1] coarse-grained IF2 Lagrangian depends on phi ONLY via grad phi (MI reads acceleration,
        not potential): L[grad(phi+phi0)] = L[grad phi].  SHIFT-SYMMETRIC.  Matches AeST. [MATCH]
[Q3.2] BUT: AeST's scalar also carries the Q=A.grad phi (TIME-gradient) sector that supplies the
        cosmological K(Q) dust (eq 3-4, the a^-3 mode driving the 3rd CMB peak). The IF2 scalar is
        a QUASISTATIC acceleration potential (Y-sector); the coarse-graining produces the Y (spatial-
        gradient) sector but NOT a dynamical Q-sector with a minimum at Q0!=0. So phi emerges with the
        right shift symmetry and the right Y-sector, but the cosmological Q-sector (the AeST 'dust')
        is NOT produced by the MI coarse-graining.  Q3 = PARTIAL: scalar+shift+Y yes, K(Q)-dust NO.

================================================================================
 Q4.  Is a0 (hence Z, kappa) PRODUCED or only matched/transmitted?
================================================================================
[Q4.1] a0 is an INPUT to the IF2 matching 2F'(x^2)=mu_fw(x): mu_fw's only scale. The coarse-graining
        TRANSMITS this same a0 into the Y^{3/2} coefficient (Q2.3). No step PRODUCES the NUMBER a0.
[Q4.2] Z=sqrt(32pi/3) and kappa=1/2 never appear in the coarse-graining algebra: a0 enters as a
        single opaque scale. The field theory inherits a0; it does not compute c^2 sqrt(Lambda/32pi).
       => Q4 = REFIT/TRANSMIT, not PRODUCE.  a0/Z/kappa quarantine INTACT (consistent w/ banked).

================================================================================
 THE MILGROM-1994 MI NO-GO (astro-ph/9303012) — does it BLOCK the join?  [verbatim]
================================================================================
Milgrom eq (10):  m*A_vec = -grad phi,  A_vec a FUNCTIONAL of the WHOLE trajectory r(t)
   (his words: 'its value is, in general, a functional of the whole trajectory').

Milgrom LOCALITY THEOREM (Sec III, verbatim): 'a theory whose kinetic action is Galilei
   invariant, and has the correct Newtonian limit, and the required MOND limit, cannot be
   local; i.e. A_vec in eq (10) cannot be a function of a finite number of time derivatives
   of r(t).'  AND (abstract): 'it is non-local in the strong sense that it cannot even be a
   limit of a sequence of local, higher-derivative theories, with increasing order.'

Milgrom eq (53)-(55): on CIRCULAR orbits the MI functional reduces to  mu(a/ao) a = dphi/dr,
   mu(a/ao)=2 v^-2 Skc(1+(1/2)Skc_hat). This is the SAME rotation-curve relation a modified-
   GRAVITY (AQUAL) theory gives. Milgrom: the two classes 'agree' on circular orbits but have
   'important applicative differences' (angular momentum invariant, disk evolution) OFF-circular.

================================================================================
   No-go bite: IF2's local-in-qddot F is the CIRCULAR (adiabatic) representative ONLY
================================================================================
[NG.1] On a NON-circular (two-frequency) trajectory, at t=0.7:
        local-theory EL inertial force = 0.342497
        target m*mu_fw(|a|/a0)*a        = -0.590220
        difference                      = 0.932716
        => NONZERO: the LOCAL-in-qddot F does NOT reproduce m*mu_fw*a off-circular.
        This IS Milgrom's no-go: a finite-derivative (local) kinetic action matches the MOND
        law only on circular/adiabatic orbits; the TRUE MI functional is irreducibly NONLOCAL.
[NG.2] On a circular orbit (|qddot|=a=const): d^2/dt^2 of (a constant) = 0  => local EL inertial force collapses to the algebraic m*mu_fw(a/a0)*a (no extra derivatives).
        => AGREE on circular orbits, DISAGREE off-circular. EXACTLY Milgrom eq(53)+no-go. [VERIFIED]

================================================================================
 THE COVARIANT-FORM BLOCK: does the no-go forbid turning IF2-MI into AeST's modified GRAVITY?
================================================================================
AeST is MODIFIED GRAVITY (Skordis-Zlosnik, verbatim): matter couples ONLY to g_mu_nu (eq 5,
   '+S_m[g]'; text: 'matter couples only to Phi'); the deep-MOND v^4=GMa0 comes from the
   modified-POISSON Y^{3/2} field term, with phi a GRAVITATING scalar (sources the metric).
IF2 is MODIFIED INERTIA: the |grad phi|^3 rides on the matter worldline kinetic term, GATED by
   mu_fw(a/a0) -> 1 wherever a>>a0 (switches OFF in the solar system).

Milgrom's no-go forbids EXACTLY this conversion in general: the MI functional (nonlocal,
   trajectory-functional A_vec) and the MG (modified-Poisson, local-in-fields) form AGREE only
   on circular orbits (eq 53). Off-circular they DIFFER (angular momentum, disk evolution). So:
   coarse-graining IF2 to a FIELD theory can reproduce AeST's STATIC RAR / circular-orbit sector
   (the Y^{3/2}/a0 slot, Q2) but CANNOT reproduce AeST as a full theory, because AeST's gravitating
   scalar is UNGATED (present at all a) whereas IF2's is mu_fw-GATED (the defining MI content).
   The conversion MI->MG is blocked by Milgrom-1994 except on the circular-orbit locus.

[GATE] mu_fw gate across scales (the switch AeST's ungated scalar does NOT have):
        Saturn (a/a0~7e5)              mu_fw=0.999999   (1-mu_fw=7.2e-07)
        galaxy outskirts (a/a0~1)      mu_fw=0.636504   (1-mu_fw=0.363)
        deep-MOND (a/a0~1e-2)          mu_fw=0.0106988   (1-mu_fw=0.989)
        => the gate spans mu_fw ~1 (solar, MI OFF, Cassini-safe) to ~0.01 (deep-MOND, MI ON).
        AeST has NO such gate on its gravitating scalar -> AeST fails Cassini; IF2 evades it.

